-- title:
--   Inertia displacement count for ℓ^k-torsion of J₀(N₀p)
-- statement:
--   Fix $N_0 \ge 1$ and a prime $p$ with $p \nmid N_0$, and let $A$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ lying over $p$ in the sense that $p$ belongs to `A.nonunits`. Let $\Lambda$ be a `LevelData` for $(N_0,p,A)$ — a section of the base over $\operatorname{Spec} A$ agreeing with the generic point, a scheme over the base with a relative group law, and bijections matching `JZero N₀` with the generic-fibre sections and the divisor class group over the residue field of $A$ with the special-fibre sections — satisfying `IsJacobian` (the abelian-scheme property bundle, commutativity and additivity of the group law on both identifications, Galois equivariance, compatibility of reduction, and realisation of Hecke operators by endomorphisms over the base), and let $O$ be a `JZeroNeronObjectAtP` over these data: a smooth, separated, locally of finite type, quasi-compact, surjective group scheme over the base with preconnected fibres, whose generic-fibre sections are identified Galois- and Hecke-equivariantly with $J =$ `JZero (N₀ * p)` $= \mathrm{Pic}^0$ of the level-$N_0p$ modular function field over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, with flat surjective multiplication-by-$n$ maps, proper generic fibre, and toric data. Let $\ell$ be a prime with $\ell \ne p$ and $k \in \mathbb N$, write $J[\ell^k]$ for the $\ell^k$-torsion subgroup of $J$, and let $I_A \subseteq \operatorname{Gal}(\overline{\mathbb Q}/\mathbb Q)$ be the image of the inertia subgroup of $A$ inside its decomposition subgroup. Assume that for every $\sigma \in I_A$ and every $x \in J[\ell^k]$ the displacement $\sigma x - x$ lies in $O.\mathrm{toricPts}(\ell^k)$, the subgroup generated by the range of the toric points of level $\ell^k$. Then $$\#J[\ell^k] \le \#S \cdot \#\bigl(J[\ell^k] \cap J^{I_A}\bigr),$$ where $S$ is the subgroup of $J$ generated by all $\sigma x - x$ with $\sigma \in I_A$ and $x \in J[\ell^k]$, and $J^{I_A}$ is the subgroup of elements fixed by every element of $I_A$.
--
--   This is the counting step in the monodromy analysis of the $\ell^k$-torsion of $J_0(N_0p)$ at a place above $p$: when all inertia displacements are toric, tameness forces $I_A$ to act through a cyclic quotient, and the order of the torsion group is bounded by the product of the order of the displacement subgroup and the order of the inertia-invariant torsion. It is used in the proof that the toric points are contained in the toric monodromy part, part of the local analysis at $p$ underlying level lowering.
